# Hostile audit — collapsed support-six corridor nonplanarity reduction

**Audited source:** `research/target_c_support6_collapsed_corridor_nonplanarity_2026-09-18.md`  
**Verdict:** PASS at the explicitly scoped conditional level  
**Theorem-state authority:** unchanged

## 1. Edge count

The collapsed degree-pure host has twelve present internal pairs because `K_6` has
fifteen pairs and the perfect matching removes three. There are six outside/activated
incidences, one at each host. Treating the outside/activated terminal as one grounded
host gives eighteen distinct skeleton edges on seven vertices.

The count is not a count of raw contact edges. It is a count of complete train
corridors under the note's contraction hypothesis. This distinction is binding.

## 2. Planarity implication

If the corridors are internally disjoint, their contraction is a minor of the planar
cellulation and produces a simple planar graph on seven vertices. The simple planar
bound `E <= 3V-6` gives `18 <= 15`, a contradiction. The argument does not use the
auxiliary genus-two quotient from the local certificate.

## 3. Crossing lower bound

For a general-position drawing of the contracted skeleton, remove one edge incident to
each crossing point. The remaining graph is planar, so at most `3V-6` edges survive.
Hence the number of crossing events is at least `18-15=3`. This is only a lower bound
on events, not on distinct train pairs; one train can participate in several crossings.

The verifier also exhausts all `6!` cyclic endpoint orders in the all-outer common-host
subcase. The internal graph has minimum convex chord-crossing count six. The cyclic
order reduction uses only pairwise noncrossing of the six parallel anchor corridors and
the common outer endpoint; it is not asserted for multiple activated hosts.

In every one of the 48 minimum orders, the six crossing pairs form a single `C_6` on
six internal train vertices, with the other six internal trains isolated. For the fixed
collapsed `+++---` label word, 36 of the orders have two cyclic sign transitions and 12
have six. This is an exact classification of the minimum pattern, not an assertion
that the pattern is impossible.

The verifier also records the colour refinement: in the 36 two-transition orders the
six crossings split as `(2,0,4)` among (cross/cross, same/same, mixed) internal-train
colour pairs; in the 12 alternating orders the split is `(0,6,0)`. This is only an
exact finite classification of the minimum interaction pattern.

## 4. Scope regression

The conclusion is not that the collapsed branch is globally impossible. The current
stopped-train model allows train corridors to share rhombi or interact at crossing
cells, and those interactions invalidate the internally-disjoint contraction premise.
The exact local collapsed realization therefore remains a binding regression against
purely local exclusions.

**Audit disposition:** PASS as a scoped global reduction. The missing theorem is now
explicit: classify or exclude the at-least-three corridor interactions under the
triangle-free train-crossing graph and the six parallel outside directions.
